cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below
  (or the version-specific metadata attached to the exact release you used).
type: software
title: "repeatMito"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
abstract: >-
  Iterative reseeding and graph-based detection of repeat-mediated
  mitochondrial genome assembly breaks from short reads alone, combining
  NOVOPlasty and GetOrganelle in an iterative, cross-validated workflow with
  Bandage-based assembly-graph depth screening. Includes a dual-lineage (DUI)
  mode for recovering divergent, co-occurring F-type and M-type mitochondrial
  genomes from a single heteroplasmic read pool in animals exhibiting Doubly
  Uniparental Inheritance.
authors:
  - family-names: "Angulo"
    given-names: "Fernanda E."
    affiliation: "Universidad Austral de Chile"
  - family-names: "Núñez"
    given-names: "José J."
    affiliation: "Universidad Austral de Chile"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LESS-UACh/repeatMito"
keywords:
  - mitochondrial genome assembly
  - doubly uniparental inheritance
  - DUI
  - NOVOPlasty
  - GetOrganelle
  - organelle genomics
  - repeat-mediated assembly
  - bioinformatics pipeline
  - molecular systematics
